{"body":"## Incident\n\nDuring the durable first-effect grant integration, review found an internal projection/recorder-shaped construction path that could create a `VERIFIED` grant record without first accepting and verifying a raw signed grant at the ingress boundary.\n\nThis is a false-green authorization-boundary defect: ordinary route and ledger checks can be green while an internal caller still has a capability-shaped path to record execution authority that is not tied to verifier acceptance and the immutable deployment output pin. No production data, credentials, or runtime endpoint information are involved.\n\n## Observed bypass shape\n\nThe reviewed construction surface exposed the capability names `ModelFirstEffectVerifiedGrantProjection`, `PostgresVerifiedFirstEffectRecorder`, and `record_verified_grant`. Those names are recorded here as identifiers only; this incident does not publish executable source or captured payloads.\n\n## Reproduction class\n\nThe captured public incident record must be rejected by the verified-grant ingress boundary validator because it records the prohibited capability shape. Production source must likewise contain none of those capability names outside the trusted composition boundary.\n\n## Corrective action\n\n- Remove public or internal projection/recorder capability surfaces for verified grants.\n- Permit the `VERIFIED` insert only from trusted composition after raw signed-wire verification and exact output-pin equality.\n- Wire `scripts/validation/validate_verified_grant_ingress_boundary.py` into pre-commit.\n- Add an incident-replay registry case so the new enforcement cannot become an unproven guard.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The boundary validator rejects the captured bypass shape.\n- Production source exposes no removed projection or recorder capability.\n- The sole `VERIFIED` insert remains within safe composition, following verifier acceptance and immutable output-pin comparison.\n- The incident-replay coverage gate recognizes this issue as the R3 record for the guard.","created_at":"2026-08-31T22:10:48Z","number":3087,"state":"open","title":"Verified first-effect grants: projection/recorder bypass could create authority rows","url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/issues/3087"}
